- Story & Context: Inspired by the shipboard urban legend of Sister Mercy—a triage nurse who reportedly lost her mind during solar transit and led a ward of feverish patients in a deadly game of Red Light, Green Light inside the spinning centrifuge hub—the EP closes on this sprawling, nine-minute dirge. The track utilizes an agonizingly slow breakbeat that completely stops whenever the brittle xylophone strikes a high, dissonant staccato chord, mimicking the terrifying stillness required by the game's lethal rules. Recorded live in the ship’s empty chapel bay with two hundred crew members holding their breath in unison, the climactic chant became an unauthorized hymn throughout the ship: "Freeze when the red diode burns your eyes."
